      "a lot of negotiation, planning, negative thoughts, judgment, a lot of saying no to old situations, a lot of stepping out of what was normal, a lot of scrutiny and strategy applied to my waking hours,",
      "a lot of mistakes and self-sabatoge, which i see now is just a part of the journey which you fight against outsmart outmaneuver and laugh about,",
      "but the steps that i did take - the dreams that i wrote down - the emotional charge i felt to not stop thinking about what i wanted most - the quiet work and hours i put in - the media i sought out and learned from - the refusal to let go of these visions.",
      "i am so so so grateful to my younger self and god.",
      "i really love life. i really am excited, for the future yes, but i’m so excited about fucking today - spending time with these older people who are all also working toward bringing their ideas to fruition. i have had many wonderful conversations already, which if you know me is in my top 10 things in life. i’m so excited for today, the workshops, the nature walk. i’m excited for tomorrow, the last morning before returning.",
      "i’m so excited to go back to my apartment in brooklyn and cook myself food, to wake up early and read my dreams and vision again, to go train and cultivate my body, to go to class and talk to the beautiful girl in my class - to let go of any fear or expectation and rather be curious about something someone beautiful - the same thing that led me to the work, the friends, the city i love. i’m so excited to go into work, my JOB, and talk about ideas that move me, to work on bringing my deepest values to life with people more experienced than me.",
      "i’m just so excited.",
      "i urge you to not stop.",
      "i urge you to structure and build and design your way of life around what moves you the most, what makes you the most excited to get up and live, and to take the obstacles and setbacks and fears and frustration and anger you experience with that with grace, with playfulness.",
      "you can do it like it’s a big weight on you or you can do it like it’s part of the dance.",
